# Example environment file for i am Architect.
#
# This is a TEMPLATE ONLY - it contains no real credentials. Copy it to
# `.env` (already gitignored - see .gitignore) and fill in real values
# for your own local/server use. Never commit a real `.env` file.
#
# Two very different kinds of variable live here - read
# src/engine/ai/README.md's "Security boundary" section before touching
# either:
#
# - OPENAI_API_KEY is a SECRET. It must only ever be supplied to a
#   trusted, server-side process - see backend/.env.example, which is
#   where it's actually used (backend/src/server.ts). Nothing in this
#   root-level file is ever read automatically by the frontend or the
#   backend; it exists purely as a documented name/place for local
#   reference. It must NEVER be prefixed "VITE_" - Vite inlines every
#   VITE_-prefixed variable, in cleartext, into the browser bundle it
#   ships to every visitor.
# - VITE_AI_BACKEND_URL is NOT a secret - it's the plain URL of the AI
#   proxy backend (see backend/README.md), read once by
#   src/main.ts via Vite's client-side `import.meta.env`. This one
#   genuinely needs the "VITE_" prefix to reach the frontend at all.

# (Not read automatically by anything in this repo - see above.) Your
# OpenAI API key. Get one at https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-api-key-here

# Base URL of the backend (backend/) that the frontend sends AI
# command-bar instructions to and saves/opens projects through. Not a
# secret - just an address. Defaults to http://localhost:8787 (the
# backend's own documented default port) if unset - see src/main.ts.
VITE_AI_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8787
